{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388529 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186388530 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388525 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "43aa64d2-1826-583b-afa1-0a5a086f07b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388526 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388526 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388526 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "659e6953-7cee-5b96-970f-fa397b86ee27" #edb/ref 175