sform into ${y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}=1$ or $‖y‖=1.$\n\nSo, introducing a change-of-coordinate matrix \n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwe obtain that $x=Py.$ Substituting this into the expression of the quadratic form, we get\n\n$$\nQ(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax=(Py)^{T}A\\,(Py)={y}^{T}\\,({P}^{T}AP)y={Q}^{′}(y).\n$$\n\nAs a result, since ${P}^{T}=P,$ the matrix of our quadratic form in new coordinates is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & ={P}^{T}\\,AP \\\\  & =PAP \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we maximize ${Q}^{′}(y)$ when $‖y‖=1,$ as usual.\n\nSince we are told that the maximum value of the quadratic form is $25,$ we have\n\n$$\nmax\\{{Q}^{′}(y)\\,|\\,‖y‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{max}=25.\n$$\n\nNext, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}=25:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-25I & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 9\\end{aligned}]-25[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & -16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(B-25I)y=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=5,$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{max}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we map this vector back to the initial coordinate  system using the change-of-coordinates matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{max}} & =P{u}_{\\text{max}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410199 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410199 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0d7e6a3a-4e90-51f7-9e6d-1f36e15dea08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410199 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410200 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3781c4aa-7e7b-5b51-9af4-d354711b0091" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410200 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410201 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410201 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "80ab5b9e-fd44-5cd4-b555-7638c14ed974" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410201 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410195 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410202 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410202 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cd806b8f-e6cf-5b59-a4ed-ccc0cfee81a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410202 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410203 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186410201 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410203 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f08afe40-e4fb-52cb-a8c1-acffe9c0cb58" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186410203 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186410198 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186414678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1045 "Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms: Determining Where Extrema are Attained" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186414677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414667 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186